# Citation metadata for tradefloor, in Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# NO DOI YET. A DOI is deliberately absent rather than invented: the fields
# `doi:` and `identifiers:` are left out until the repository is deposited to
# Zenodo, which mints one per release and one concept DOI for the project as a
# whole. That deposit is the next step for citability, and when it happens the
# `doi:` field and a `date-released:` for the tagged version belong here.
#
# `version:` tracks the `version` field in pyproject.toml, and
# `date-released:` is the day that version was tagged. Both move together at
# a release; a version without the date it shipped is half a citation.
#
# A citation identifies the software. A run is identified by its RunManifest,
# which carries the roster, the macro initial conditions, the scenario, the
# order log and the strategy, with the package version, the preset and the
# digest a replay has to reproduce. The manifest is documented at
# https://tradefloor.dev/evaluate.html#runmanifest, and the citation guidance
# is at https://tradefloor.dev/install.html#citing-tradefloor.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: tradefloor
abstract: >-
  A deterministic market simulator with a real limit order book. A Rust core
  with a Python API. The same seed produces the same market on every platform,
  every price move carries a labelled factor decomposition, and orders match
  against depth so trading moves the price.
type: software
authors:
